00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:18.250 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  since the franchises reboot in 2013  we've been excited for Crystal Dynamics  next Tomb Raider game the last game  showed heroine Lara Croft facing  impossible odds odds that would  eventually inspire her to seek adventure  now with Rises the Tomb Raider we get  the chance to see Lara come into her own  and watch her grow into the hardcore  archaeologist she's destined to be we  sat down with the game's director brain  Horton to talk about the changes to Lara  and her world which already sound like  huge improvements over the last game  players have more tools available to  them and facing a situation including  new traversal areas like trees and water  objects in the environment that can be  crafted into weapons and an expanded  skill tree that allows you to customize  Lara to your own unique combat  we've really wanted to build on the  foundation that we had in Tomb Raider  2013 and we had a combination of  straight-up action and we called it pre  combat or light stealth so a lot of  people responded very well to that and  we doubled down on it we came up with  what we call the guerrilla combat style  and that includes new traversal  mechanics like climbing on trees or  swimming underwater to evade detection  and also to perform the silent kills  from from above below  the other thing we've added in guerrilla  combat are a lot more tools and  makeshift weapons so you're gonna see  bottles and cans in the world those  things that can be used for distractions  but they also be crafted and used as  weapons so the it's the combination of  being able to use your traversal use  your mobility and get the upper hand on  the enemy combatants and then creating  distractions and chaos with the weapons  and tools that you have in the world we  wanted to make sure the player at  anytime had a strategic choice and they  can look at the situation and make a  decision either based on their play  style or how they wanted to go about it  if they're low on resources and they  want to get through a section they can  go completely stealth and not be seen  we've increased the amount of things in  the world that you can collect so we try  to make them as contextualise as  possible for for the bows you can you  can collect cloth and you can collect  wood and you can collect mushrooms these  different things can be crafted in  different formulas to create very cool  ammunition like the poison arrow being  one of them not only can you make a  poison arrow but you can make well you  know a skill upgrade you can make a  poison bomb so you can take get a corpse  you can create this this poison bomb on  the corpse and it will attract an enemy  AI to it or make a beeping sound and  then it'll explode right when they come  up to it it's all systemic we try as  much as possible to give the combat  designers an AI that allows them to  craft scenarios and situations not  setups and and there are moments where  you want to have a very clear this  happens then that happens but there's  also moments where we want them to be on  patrol patterns and and going through  what we call a need system that they  have a need to want to go to see a  location or if it's raining that they  might want to get into shelter that  makes the AI feel a lot more responsive  and reactive to the world  mobility was the foundation of Tomb  Raider 2013 our cover system was what we  called fluid cover so she would never  get stuck to a surface she could just  contextually crouched near cover  surfaces but now we've increased that we  have the ability to be up in the trees  and being bushes can be underwater all  of these have certain ability to get the  top of the enemy's awareness cones  but once again you can make noises and  you can pop that bubble and then a I  will be aware of you those bushes will  no longer be a valid hiding spot  we want to encourage creativity and  improvisation if they want to go  vertical they can do that if they wanted  to take a low path they can so we really  want to open up the play space let the  player observe the patterns of the a I  see what they're doing and make  adjustments to to get through that the  sequence the way they want to  this is the most metal gear we've ever  seen Lara Croft we're watching her  become the Tomb Raider using both her  archaeological smarts and physical  prowess to solve puzzles overcome  obstacles and become a true force to be  reckoned with there are so many ways to  attack situations giving players the  opportunity to tailor their play style  stealth all the way or running gun  alright  Tomb Raider you've set our expectations  extremely high let's see if you can rise  to the occasion

